title: dragging Operator
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

The <<.olink dragging>> operator answers whether the user is dragging something at this moment. It is true for any drag, wherever it started and whatever is being dragged. See DragAndDropMechanism for an overview.

The answer is the one that holds at the moment the filter is evaluated. Nothing is re-evaluated when a drag begins or ends, so this operator is meant for filters that are already being evaluated because of the drag, rather than for deciding what to show at rest.

The drag is still counted as under way while a drop is being handled, because it does not end until after the drop. A condition written instead against the state tiddlers a drag keeps would go false too early, since those are usually deleted as part of handling the drop.

! Examples

The AnimateLayoutWidget uses it to animate a list only while it is being reordered by dragging, leaving the animations that run at other times undisturbed:

```
<$animatelayout list="$:/StoryList" enable={{{ [dragging[]] }}}>
```
